    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0136" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg970"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/603b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-07T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6797. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 165. Supplementing and amending Nos. 113 and 154.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d55-f1"/> We proposed issuing with discretion “Z” licenses without
                    reference to London for: <pb facs="0137" n="971" xml:id="pg971"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Reasonable quantities of any commodities for the Diplomatic, Consular,
                            Army and Navy officials of the United States and of any friendly
                            country;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Personal effects, household goods, and other small articles of
                            personal property of similar character;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Samples of commodities of all kinds including commodities that may be
                            on the embargo list providing they are of no commercial value;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Articles of small value used solely for advertising purposes provided
                            they are consigned to the American Consul at point of destination for
                            purpose of censorship;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Foodstuffs consigned to the citizens of the United States and the
                            Allied countries sojourning abroad, not exceeding $20 in value for any
                            one shipment.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>It is proposed to issue these “Z” licenses only in exceptional cases. We propose
                    issuing such licenses immediately. We have consulted the British Embassy, who
                    have agreed, subject to approval from the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
